<title>USA: Alpha Microsystems sees Q2 write-off.</title>
<headline>Alpha Microsystems sees Q2 write-off.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA ANA, Calif. 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alpha Microsystems said Tuesday it expects to take a one-time write-off of up to $200,000 in the second quarter for the sale of its Alpha HealthCare unit.</p>
<p>The company said it signed a letter of intent to sell the unit to privately held Datacon Management Inc for a combination of cash, notes and other consideration.</p>
<p>Further financial terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The transaction is subject to the signing of a definitive agreement and completion of due diligence.</p>
<p>The sale is expected to close within 30 days.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
